  "description": "Compare two strings S and T. '#' represents a backspace character. Return true if they are equal after processing backspaces.",
  "pseudocode": "function backspaceCompare(S, T) {\n  const build = (s) => {\n    let res = [];\n    for (let char of s) {\n      if (char !== '#') res.push(char);\n      else res.pop();\n    }\n    return res.join('');\n  };\n  return build(S) === build(T);\n}",
